WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
The Merchant of Venice is
packed with big speeches.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.420
Pleas.

3
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.420
Insults.

4
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.420
Warnings.

5
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.650
A whole speech about mercy.

6
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.350
Each one is built to win somebody over:
"The quality of mercy is not strain’d,"

7
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.740
Now put a meter over the
people each speech is aimed at.

8
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.570
Does anyone change their mind?

9
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.100
Every speech tries.

10
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.370
So which ones actually work?

11
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.920
In this mission, you'll hear the
difference between verse and prose,

12
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.870
and who switches between them.

13
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.330
You'll name the tools of
persuasion: rhetorical questions,

14
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.240
repetition, antithesis and imagery.

15
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.450
And you'll catch Antonio warning: "The
devil can cite Scripture for his purpose."

16
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.820
Your mission: decide which of
the big speeches really persuade.
